<p>
I make lots of little <a href="https://emacsconf.org/2026/talks">EmacsConf schedule</a> updates based on the speakers' feedback.
I needed a way to keep track of the schedule that I've just sent the speaker so that I could calculate the differences and notify them again the next time I change the schedule for their talk.
I like the way that keeping track of this lets me include a summary of the change in the subject and in the body of the message. For example, one of the emails I sent today had the subject:
This blog post is about updating the <code>EMAILED_SCHEDULE</code> entry property in my Org Mode file that keeps track of this year's conference talks so that I can save the schedule that I've emailed. I want to set it only after I've successfully sent the email, because I might change my mind or forget to send the e-mail, and I want to make sure the entry property is based on what I've e-mailed.
</p>

<pre class="example" id="org1929970">
EmacsConf 2026: Schedule update as of 2026-10-28: svg: Sun ~2:20 PM EST (40 min earlier)
</pre>

<p>
I send the messages within Emacs, of course. This lets me use <a href="https://git.emacsconf.org/emacsconf-el/tree/emacsconf-mail.el">emacsconf-mail.el</a> to mail-merge using Emacs Lisp. I can then use <code>message-sent-hook</code> to run buffer-specific code once I've sent the message. This lets me set it up so that each message updates its own talk once I've used <code>C-c C-c</code> to send it.
</p>

<p>
First, I need a function that adds to a talk's logbook.
This is not specifically needed for the <code>message-sent-hook</code>, but it's useful for keeping track of the fact that I've sent this kind of email to that speaker on this date.
It's very helpful to be able to see who I've already sent the backstage information to or when was the last time I sent them a schedule update.
I can also filter the list of talks by the text in the logs so that if I partially send a mail merge and then cancel the rest because I want to tweak the code, I can send the new mail merge only to the remaining speakers.
This is in <a href="https://git.emacsconf.org/emacsconf-el/tree/emacsconf.el">emacsconf.el</a>.
</p>

<p>
</p><details><summary>emacsconf-add-to-talk-logbook: Add NOTE as a logbook entry for TALK.</summary><div class="org-src-container"><pre class="src src-emacs-lisp">(<span class="org-keyword">defun</span> <span class="org-function-name">emacsconf-add-to-talk-logbook</span> (talk note)
  <span class="org-doc">"Add NOTE as a logbook entry for TALK."</span>
  (<span class="org-keyword">interactive</span> (list (emacsconf-complete-talk) (read-string <span class="org-string">"Note: "</span>)))
  (<span class="org-keyword">save-window-excursion</span>
    (<span class="org-keyword">save-excursion</span>
      (<span class="org-keyword">emacsconf-with-talk-heading</span> talk
        (emacsconf-add-to-logbook
         (<span class="org-keyword">if</span> (functionp note)
             (funcall note)
           note))
        (bury-buffer (current-buffer))))))

</pre></div></details>
<p></p>

<p>
This function is the one that gets added to the message sent hook. It's in <a href="https://git.emacsconf.org/emacsconf-el/tree/emacsconf-mail.el">emacsconf-mail.el</a>:
</p>

<p>
</p><details><summary>emacsconf-mail-add-to-logbook: Add to logbook for all matching talks from this speaker.</summary><div class="org-src-container"><pre class="src src-emacs-lisp">(<span class="org-keyword">defun</span> <span class="org-function-name">emacsconf-mail-add-to-logbook</span> (email note)
  <span class="org-doc">"Add to logbook for all matching talks from this speaker."</span>
  (<span class="org-keyword">interactive</span>
   (<span class="org-keyword">let*</span> ((email (mail-strip-quoted-names
                  (plist-get (plist-get (notmuch-show-get-message-properties) <span class="org-builtin">:headers</span>)
                             <span class="org-builtin">:From</span>)))
          (talks (emacsconf-mail-talks email)))
     (list
      email
      (read-string (format <span class="org-string">"Note for %s: "</span>
                           (mapconcat (<span class="org-keyword">lambda</span> (o) (plist-get o <span class="org-builtin">:slug</span>))
                                      talks<span class="org-string">", "</span>))))))
  (<span class="org-keyword">condition-case</span> e
      (<span class="org-keyword">save-window-excursion</span>
        (mapc
         (<span class="org-keyword">lambda</span> (talk)
           (emacsconf-add-to-talk-logbook talk note))
         (emacsconf-mail-talks email)))
    (<span class="org-warning">error</span> (message <span class="org-string">"Error %s"</span> e))))

</pre></div></details>
<p></p>

<p>
And this function actually sets up the <code>message-sent-hook</code>:
</p>

<p>
</p><details><summary>emacsconf-mail-log-message-when-sent</summary><div class="org-src-container"><pre class="src src-emacs-lisp">(<span class="org-keyword">defun</span> <span class="org-function-name">emacsconf-mail-log-message-when-sent</span> (o message)
  (add-hook <span class="org-highlight-quoted-quote">'</span><span class="org-highlight-quoted-symbol">message-sent-hook</span>
            <span class="org-highlight-quoted-quote">`</span>(<span class="org-keyword">lambda</span> ()
               (<span class="org-keyword">save-window-excursion</span>
                 (emacsconf-add-to-talk-logbook
                  ,(plist-get o <span class="org-builtin">:slug</span>)
                  ,message))
               (<span class="org-keyword">when</span> (match-buffers <span class="org-string">"*unsent"</span>)
                 (switch-to-buffer (car (match-buffers <span class="org-string">"*unsent"</span>)))))
            nil t))

</pre></div></details>
<p></p>

<p>
Which gets called by this part of <code>emacsconf-mail-prepare</code>:
</p>


<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-emacs-lisp"><code>(<span class="org-keyword">when</span> (plist-get template <span class="org-builtin">:log-note</span>)
  (mapc (<span class="org-keyword">lambda</span> (talk)
          (emacsconf-mail-log-message-when-sent talk (plist-get template <span class="org-builtin">:log-note</span>)))
        (emacsconf-mail-talks email)))
</code></pre>
</div>


<p>
Then my <code>emacsconf-mail-interim-schedule-update</code> can specify the <code>:log-note</code> like this:
</p>


<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-emacs-lisp"><code>      <span class="org-builtin">:log-note</span>
      (<span class="org-keyword">lambda</span> ()
        (<span class="org-keyword">dolist</span> (talk (cdr group))
          (<span class="org-keyword">emacsconf-with-talk-heading</span> talk
            (emacsconf-schedule-save-emailed-time)))
        (concat <span class="org-string">"emacsconf-mail-interim-schedule-update"</span>
                (<span class="org-keyword">if</span> log-note (concat <span class="org-string">": "</span> log-note) <span class="org-string">""</span>) <span class="org-string">" - "</span> summary))
</code></pre>
</div>


<p>
This lets me run that code only when the mail gets sent.
</p>

